      question: 'Your app slows down: profiling shows hundreds of components re-render on every keystroke in a search box whose value lives in context. Fix it.',
      answer: 'Root cause: every context consumer re-renders on every provider value change, and a keystroke-frequency value in context is maximal blast radius — memo cannot block it. Fixes, in order: (1) move the input state local and only publish debounced/committed values upward; (2) split contexts so the hot value is isolated from cold ones (and memoize provider value objects); (3) for genuinely shared hot state, use a subscription store (zustand/jotai/redux) where components select slices and only re-render when THEIR slice changes — implemented on useSyncExternalStore.',
      deepDive: 'Explain WHY stores escape the problem: the store object in context (or module scope) never changes identity; components subscribe with selectors, and the store notifies only matching subscribers — granularity that vanilla context lacks by design.',
